    resource 0x7f13008a string/agreement_serious_content PUBLIC
      () "<p><b>Movness 用户协议与隐私说明</b><br>版本：2026-11-06-movness；适用于本次开发预览版。</p>
      <p><b>1. 产品与提供方式</b><br>Movness 是基于开源组件开发的个人行动助手，提供手机任务交互及可选的电脑协作。此预览版由向你提供安装包的项目维护者交付；反馈、纠错或数据处理问题请通过原交付渠道联系。它不是上游项目的官方发行版。开源组件的作者、许可证与来源见「关于」及交接源码，适用许可证赋予你的权利不因本说明而减少。</p>
      <p><b>2. 任务、权限与结果</b><br>模型、系统权限、工具授权及电脑配对分别决定可用能力。开启某项系统权限并不表示授权任意目的的操作。用户提出目标后，助手可以在授权范围内连续使用工具。电脑配对须由电脑端确认；任务已接收、模型已回复与成果文件已保存是不同状态。应用不保证模型判断正确或每次任务成功；不应仅凭模型宣称完成认定结果。</p>
      <p><b>3. 本机数据与保存</b><br>聊天、角色配置、记忆、模型配置及相关凭据通常保存在应用私有数据中，取回的电脑成果也保存到本机。导出、分享和备份会在你选择的位置生成副本。应用未对所有配置和 API 凭据作统一加密承诺；请结合设备锁屏与系统安全设置保管。数据通常保留到你删除对应记录、清除应用数据或卸载；外部存储、备份和第三方端的副本不随之自动删除。</p>
      <p><b>4. 网络请求与接收方</b><br>使用云模型时，当前对话及构造请求所需的提示、工具结果、文件或情境信息会发送到所配置的模型端点，该端点可能由模型厂商或你选择的中转服务运营。语音、搜索、绘图、MCP、插件市场、更新和 GitHub 等功能会访问各自的服务。电脑协作将任务发送给已配对的电脑服务，并读取会话或指定成果文件；电脑端还可能调用其配置的模型。上述接收方各自的数据规则适用。位置、日程、屏幕或文件访问取决于任务、所启用的工具及系统权限；此版本不承诺持续感知或全天候无人值守。</p>
      <p><b>5. 用户选择与数据管理</b><br>你可以更换模型端点、关闭工具或系统权限、撤销电脑连接、删除记录及导出可用的数据。撤销连接会停止后续授权访问，不自动删除已取回的本地文件。手机停止只结束当前手机回合；电脑取消作用于所选电脑会话。删除、对外发送、发布及其他设备变更应符合用户授权，重要内容请保留可恢复副本。</p>
      <p><b>6. 扩展与软件边界</b><br>第三方插件、脚本、Skill、模型和电脑服务由各自作者或提供者负责。显示在应用中不表示由 Movness 开发、运营或背书。市场服务与公开仓库的实际运营方以原始来源为准。软件处于开发预览阶段，输出和自动化可能失败；各方责任依适用法律、实际行为及相应许可证处理，本说明不免除依法不得免除的责任。</p>
      <p><b>7. 版本与确认</b><br>本说明在应用中提供。数据处理或用户权益发生实质变化时，应更新协议版本并在继续使用相关功能前说明。本次确认针对 Movness 预览版，不代表同意未说明的新用途；你可以拒绝并退出。</p>"
      (id) "<p><b>Movness user agreement and privacy notice</b><br>Version: 2026-11-06-movness; this development preview.</p>
      <p><b>1. Product and provider</b><br>Movness is a personal action assistant built on open-source components, with phone interactions and optional computer collaboration. The project maintainer who supplied this preview is your feedback and data-handling contact through the original delivery channel. This is not an official upstream release. See About and the source handoff for upstream authors, licences and origins; their licence rights remain intact.</p>
      <p><b>2. Tasks and permissions</b><br>Model configuration, Android permissions, tool grants and computer pairing determine available capabilities separately. An Android permission is not authorization for arbitrary purposes. Tools may run continuously within the authorized task. Pairing requires approval on the computer. Task accepted, model replied and file retrieved are distinct states. A model completion statement alone is not proof of success.</p>
      <p><b>3. Local storage and retention</b><br>Chats, character settings, memory, model settings and credentials are generally stored in private app data, as are retrieved computer results. Export, sharing and backup create copies at chosen locations. This release makes no blanket claim that all settings or API credentials are encrypted. Records normally remain until deleted, app data is cleared or the app is uninstalled. Exported files, backups and third-party copies require separate management.</p>
      <p><b>4. Requests and recipients</b><br>Cloud model endpoints receive the conversation, prompts, tool output and files or context needed to construct the request. Endpoints may be model vendors or relays selected by you. Voice, search, image generation, MCP, markets, updates and GitHub use their respective services. Computer tasks go to the paired service, which may use its own configured model. Each recipient has its own data rules. Location, calendar, screen and file access depend on tools, the task and Android permission. Continuous sensing or unattended 24-hour operation is not promised.</p>
      <p><b>5. Your controls</b><br>Change endpoints, disable tools or Android permissions, revoke computer access, delete records and export available data. Revocation does not delete files already retrieved. Phone Stop ends the phone turn; computer cancellation applies to the selected computer session. Deleting, sending, publishing and other device changes must follow your authorization.</p>
      <p><b>6. Third parties and limits</b><br>Third-party extensions, models and computer services belong to their respective authors or providers. An entry in Movness does not imply Movness ownership, operation or endorsement. Original sources identify actual market and repository operators. Preview software, output and automation may fail. Liability follows applicable law, actual conduct and licences; this notice does not exclude non-waivable obligations.</p>
      <p><b>7. Changes and acceptance</b><br>This notice is available in the app. Material changes to data processing or user rights require a new version and an explanation before the affected use. Acceptance concerns this disclosed preview, not unspecified future purposes. You may decline and exit.</p>"
